\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\i0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 Invoked when the cursor leaves a cell but before the string value of the cell's object is displayed. Return YES to allow display of the string and NO to reject display and return the cursor to the cell. This method gives the delegate the opportunity to validate the contents of 
\i control
\i0 's cell (or selected cell). In validating, the delegate checks 
\i object
\i0  to determine if it falls within a permissible range, has required attributes, accords with a given context, and so on. An example of an object subject to such and evaluation is an NSDate object which should not represent a future date, or a monetary amount (represented by an NSNumber) that exceeds a predetermined limit.\

